            "y_max": 0.419,
            "width": 0.1623,
            "height": 0.1003
          },
          "confidence": 0.7598
        },
        {
          "text": "Frogs can live both on land and in freshwater and belong to class Amphibia\nof phylum Chordata. The most common species of frog found in India is\nRana tigrina.",
          "bbox": {
            "x_min": 0.3006,
            "y_min": 0.4062,
            "x_max": 0.927,
            "y_max": 0.4533,
            "width": 0.6264,
            "height": 0.0471
          },
          "confidence": 0.9953
        },
        {
          "text": "They do not have constant body temperature i.e., their body\ntemperature varies with the temperature of the environment. Such animals\nare called cold blooded or poikilotherms. You might have also noticed\nchanges in the colour of the frogs while they are in grasses and on dry\nland. They have the ability to change the colour to hide them from their\nenemies (camouflage). This protective coloration is called mimicry. You\nmay also know that frogs are not seen during peak summer and winter.\nDuring this period they take shelter in deep burrows to protect them\nfrom extreme heat and cold. This is known as summer sleep (aestivation)\nand winter sleep (hibernation) respectively.",
          "bbox": {
            "x_min": 0.3012,
            "y_min": 0.4572,
            "x_max": 0.9264,
            "y_max": 0.626,
            "width": 0.6252,
            "height": 0.1688
          },
          "confidence": 0.9959
        },
        {
