        },
        {
          "text": "canal. Finally it communicates with the urinogenital duct that comes out\nof the kidneys and opens into the cloaca. The cloaca is a small, median\nchamber that is used to pass faecal matter, urine and sperms to the exterior.",
          "bbox": {
            "x_min": 0.3018,
            "y_min": 0.1345,
            "x_max": 0.9264,
            "y_max": 0.1795,
            "width": 0.6246,
            "height": 0.045
          },
          "confidence": 0.9962
        },
        {
          "text": "The female reproductive organs include a pair of ovaries (Figure 7.4).\nThe ovaries are situated near kidneys and there is no functional connection\nwith kidneys. A pair of oviduct arising from the ovaries opens into the\ncloaca separately. A mature female can lay 2500 to 3000 ova at a time.\nFertilisation is external and takes place in water. Development involves a\nlarval stage called tadpole. Tadpole undergoes metamorphosis to form\nthe adult.",
          "bbox": {
            "x_min": 0.3006,
            "y_min": 0.1825,
            "x_max": 0.9264,
            "y_max": 0.2892,
            "width": 0.6258,
            "height": 0.1067
          },
          "confidence": 0.996
        },
        {
          "text": "Frogs are beneficial for mankind because they eat insects and protect\nthe crop. Frogs maintain ecological balance because these serve as an\nimportant link of food chain and food web in the ecosystem. In some\ncountries the muscular legs of frog are used as food by ma",
          "bbox": {
            "x_min": 0.3018,
            "y_min": 0.2948,
            "x_max": 0.9259,
            "y_max": 0.3565,
            "width": 0.6241,
            "height": 0.0617
          },
          "confidence": 0.9971
        },
        {
          "text": "SUMMARY",
          "bbox": {
            "x_min": 0.5668,
            "y_min": 0.3903,
            "x_max": 0.6614,
            "y_max": 0.4032,
            "width": 0.0946,
            "height": 0.0129
          },
          "confidence": 0.9548
        },
        {
          "text": "Cells, tissues, organs and organ systems\nthe work in a way that\nensures the survival of the body as a whole and exhibit division of labour.\nA tissue is defined as group of cells along with intercellular substances\nperforming one or more functions in the body. Epithelia are sheet like\ntissues lining the body's surface and its cavities, ducts and tubes. Epithelia\nhave one free surface facing a body fluid or the outside environment.\nTheir cells are structurally and functionally connected at junctions.",
          "bbox": {
            "x_min": 0.3012,
            "y_min": 0.4327,
            "x_max": 0.9264,
            "y_max": 0.5428,
            "width": 0.6252,
