        },
        {
          "text": "In som",
          "bbox": {
            "x_min": 0.8482,
            "y_min": 0.3098,
            "x_max": 0.9165,
            "y_max": 0.3539,
            "width": 0.0683,
            "height": 0.0441
          },
          "confidence": 0.9326
        },
        {
          "text": "The Indian bullfrog, Rana tigrina, is the common frog found in India.\nBody is covered by skin. Mucous glands are present in the skin which is\nhighly vascularised and helps in respiration in water and on land. Body is\ndivisible into head and trunk. A muscular tongue is present, which is bilobed\nat the tip and is used in capturing the prey. The alimentary canal consists\nof oesophagous, stomach, intestine and rectum, which open into the cloaca.\nThe main digestive glands are liver and pancreas. It can respire in water\nthrough skin and through lungs on land. Circulatory system is closed\nwith single circulation. RBCs are nucleated. Nervous system is organised\ninto central, peripheral and autonomic. The organs of urinogenital system\nare kidneys and urinogenital ducts, which open into the cloaca. The male\nrepro\nreproductive organ is a pair of testes. The female reproductive organ is a\npair of ovaries. A female lays 2500-3000 ova at a time. The fertilisation and\ndevelopment are external. The eggs hatch into tadpoles, which\nmetamorphose into frogs.",
